  "actor": "HARNESS",
  "what": "problem PD-1@v1 drafted",
  "phase": "DISCOVER",
  "minute": 55.0,
  "event_seq": 99,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets have roughly doubled since August 2026 (from ~600/month in Jun-Jul to 1180-1260/month in Aug-Sep, E-06), and the dominant driver is a billing import/validation defect producing incorrect bills on ACTUAL-read accounts rather than ticket-response speed (E-01 shows response times within SLA) or estimated-read substitution from field/AMI issues (E-04 shows disputed bills are dominated by ACTUAL reads, 1785 vs 1240 ESTIMATED, and E-03 rules out a tariff change). The pattern is consistent with H-BILLING-RULE-CHANGE: a change to billing import validation rules around August introduced systematic errors on correctly-read bills, which has not yet been directly confirmed against the billing-config rule change log."
 },
