  "root_problem": "Billing dispute tickets roughly doubled since August 2026 (610/590 per month Jun/Jul to 1180/1260 Aug/Sep, E-06). The confirmed mechanism behind the ESTIMATED-read dispute population (1240, matching E-04) is validation rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01 (E-13), which compares raw AMI register values to 12-month m3 history with unit_scaling='none' and so misclassifies valid high-consumption reads from v4.2-firmware meters (reporting in 0.1 m3 units, not m3, E-14) as anomalous, rejecting 1184 of them at billing import and forcing estimate substitution (E-12); whether the same rule/unit mismatch also explains the larger ACTUAL-read population (1785, E-04) is not yet established."
